    "objid": "0002",
    "raw": "The todo web viewer (`todo.py web`) renders prose fields as escaped plain text or `<pre>` blocks. Grooming and agents write markdown in Body, LongSummary, AC, State notes, and work-item commit messages; readers should be able to toggle each field between raw source and a rendered preview without leaving the page.\n\n## Grooming decision (JS, not npm)\n\nThe viewer is self-contained Python + inline JS (`todo_web.py`); there is no frontend build. Any JavaScript solution must ship inside the dumped HTML (`--dump-html`) and work offline.\n\n| Option | Size | Fit |\n|--------|------|-----|\n| Inline regex/line parser (h1-h3, bold, code, links, lists) | ~1-2 KB in `_TODO_SCRIPT` | Best default: zero deps, matches \"quick-and-dirty\" fallback |\n| Vendored snarkdown UMD (~2 KB) as a Python string or sibling `.js` file | ~2 KB | Full basic MD if we want more than headings |\n| marked / markdown-it via CDN | 12-40 KB + network | Rejected: breaks offline dump, adds runtime dependency |\n| Python `markdown` pip dep, server-only render | N/A | Rejected: toggle needs client-side raw text; server render alone cannot flip per field without round-trips |\n\n**Chosen approach:** client-side toggle per markdown-capable field using a small inline JS renderer (headings, paragraphs, `code`, links, simple lists). Start with regex/line rules; extract to vendored snarkdown only if gaps show up in real todos.\n\n## Fields in scope\n\n- Body, LongSummary (dedicated sections)\n- AC and other prose in Fields (`_meta_html`)\n- State `note` metadata\n- Work-item commit message in the fold pane\n\nSummary title stays plain (single line). JSON/meta values stay `<pre>` JSON. Diffs stay monospace.\n\n## UX\n\n- Each in-scope field gets a small \"Preview\" / \"Raw\" control in its section header (or fold header for work items).\n- Default: Raw (preserves current behavior); preference can persist in `sessionStorage` per field kind if cheap.\n- Preview pane uses `.md-preview` styles (headings, lists, `pre code`); XSS-safe via escape-then-markup pattern (never assign raw HTML from todo text without escaping user content outside allowed tags)."
  },
